        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "8934e861-8eb2-5843-a154-fddaa1e5648b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Josephine de Reszke, Mme. Nissen-Salomon, Ambroise Thomas, Michel Carré, Jules Barbier, Alexandre Dumas, père, Paul Meurice, William Shakespeare\n- Works: Hamlet (opera), Hamlet (play)\n- Places: Paris\n- Topics: music study, opera debut, composition, libretto adaptation\n\nFacts:\n- Hamlet is a five-act grand opera from 1868 composed by Ambroise Thomas.\n- The libretto of Hamlet was written by Michel Carré and Jules Barbier.\n- Hamlet was based on a French adaptation by Alexandre Dumas, père, and Paul Meurice of William Shakespeare's play Hamlet.\n- Josephine de Reszke began her studies with her mother and with Mme. Nissen-Salomon.\n- On 21 June 1875, Josephine de Reszke made her debut in Paris as Ophelia in Hamlet.",
